    axes: { harm: 1, pitch: 1, ornament: 2, meter: 1, density: 1, transmission: 1, improv: 1, soundTech: 1, intensity: 1, voice: 2, timbre: 1, percussion: 2, cyclicity: 1 },
    description: 'Australian hip-hop tradition crystallizing in 2000s through Hilltop Hoods (Adelaide), Bliss n Eso, the Herd, and the broader Obese Records-and-Elefant-Traks label rosters. Characterized by sample-based East-Coast-American-influenced production, distinct Australian-accent vocal-delivery, and explicit Australian-suburban-cultural lyrical content. Hilltop Hoods\' 2003 The Calling and 2006 The Hard Road consolidated the canonical commercial visibility.',
