    axes: { harm: 1, pitch: 1, ornament: 1, meter: 1, density: 2, transmission: 1, improv: 1, soundTech: 1, intensity: 1, voice: 1, timbre: 1, percussion: 2, cyclicity: 2 },
    description: '1990s house subgenre developed in New York and Chicago characterized by heavy world-percussion sampling (Afro-Cuban congas, African djembe-and-talking-drum, Brazilian batucada), tribal-chant vocal-sampling, and minimalist-melodic-percussion-focused arrangement. Junior Vasquez, Danny Tenaglia, Roger Sanchez, and the Sound Factory NYC scene defined the canonical 1990s tribal house aesthetic.',
