    axes: { harm: 1, pitch: 1, ornament: 1, meter: 1, density: 2, transmission: 1, improv: 1, soundTech: 1, intensity: 2, voice: -2, timbre: 1, percussion: 2, cyclicity: 1 },
    description: 'Mid-to-late-2000s house subgenre characterized by aggressive distorted-synth-lead production, heavy compression, four-on-the-floor beat with prominent off-beat bass, and explicit big-room festival-targeting. Justice\'s Cross (2007), Daft Punk\'s Discovery-influenced production legacy, and the broader French house lineage anchored the canonical aesthetic. The genre spawned the broader EDM-festival era of 2008-2012.',
    exemplars: ['Justice', 'Daft Punk', 'Boys Noize', 'Mstrkrft', 'Erol Alkan', 'Ed Banger Records'],
    status: 'documented',
    crossRefs: ['distortedRock.metal.thrash', 'experimentalElec.industrialNoise'],
