    description: '2000s and 2010s UK electronic subgenre developed through Ghost Box Records (founded 2004 by Julian House and Jim Jupp) and the broader UK-electronic scene, characterized by sampling-and-evocation of 1960s-1970s BBC Radiophonic Workshop, library music, and lost-British-television-soundtrack aesthetics. Belbury Poly, The Focus Group, The Advisory Circle, Mordant Music, and Boards of Canada (parallel adjacent) anchor the canonical hauntology roster.',
