    description: 'Late-2000s electronic subgenre invented by Dave Nada in 2009 (a chopped-and-screwed slowed-down house remix played at 110 BPM produced the canonical moombahton sound), characterized by slow-tempo (108-115 BPM) house-derived production with explicit reggaeton dembow-rhythm absorption. Major Lazer, Munchi, Dillon Francis, and the broader Mad Decent and T&A Records label rosters anchor the canonical roster. The 2011-2014 EDM commercial peak brought moombahton into festival mainstream visibility.',
