    description: 'Late-1980s and 1990s American heavy-rock subgenre integrating industrial-electronic-production with rock-band-instrumentation. Nine Inch Nails (Trent Reznor, Cleveland 1988-onward) is the canonical type-specimen with Pretty Hate Machine (1989) and The Downward Spiral (1994); Ministry (Chicago, parallel scene), Filter, Stabbing Westward, Marilyn Manson (industrial-rock-glam-hybrid), and the broader Nothing Records and TVT Records label rosters anchor the canonical industrial rock roster.',
