    description: 'The Greek nanourisma (νανούρισμα, cradle-song) tradition continuous from Byzantine-era cradle-song practice through Ottoman-period folksong survival into modern Greek domestic practice; defined by characteristic Greek-Eastern modal vocabulary (the dromos system shared with rebetiko including Hijaz and Houzam), free-meter or rocking ⁶⁄₈ phrasing, melismatic ornament with characteristic Byzantine-chant-derived microtonal inflection in older variants, demotic-Greek text register coexisting with regional dialect (Cretan, Pontic, Cypriot) survival, intimate maternal-and-grandmother singing context. Regional variants include the Cretan nanourisma (with Cretan-lyra-adjacent modal color) and the Pontic Greek (Black Sea diaspora) variants.',
    exemplars: ['"Nani nani to paidi mou" (traditional)', '"Koimisou astri" (Cretan traditional)', 'Domna Samiou — traditional cradle-song recordings (1960s-1970s)', 'Sotiria Bellou — folk-cradle recordings', 'Pontic Greek "Aliki nani"'],
    crossRefs: ['lullaby.middleEastern', 'balladPoetry.mediterraneanBallad', 'ritualDevotional.christianGospel'],
