    description: 'The Trinidadian Carnival Panorama steelpan-orchestra competition tradition continuous from 1963 first Panorama-competition founding through 20th-21st century continuous competitive performance into modern Trinidad-and-Tobago Carnival annual Panorama; the steelpan-orchestra (40-100 panmen-and-panwomen organized into tenor-pan, double-second, guitar-pan, cello-pan, six-bass sections) performs a single arranged calypso/soca tune in 8-12 minute concert-piece arrangement competing for the National Panorama Champion title (the canonical victors include Renegades, Desperadoes, Phase II Pan Groove, Despers, Trinidad All Stars). Defined by all-steel-pan-ensemble arrangement (the steel pan tuned-chromatic 12-TET pitched-percussion-vocabulary), instrumental-only no-vocal-content, complex multi-section arrangement-and-counterpoint-and-improvised-soloing.',
