    description: 'The Vietnamese hò (work-coordination call-and-response song) tradition continuous from premodern Vietnamese-agricultural-and-maritime labor practice through 19th-20th century continuous performance into modern Vietnamese-folk-revival practice across Northern, Central, and Southern Vietnam; the hò is the canonical Vietnamese work-coordination song-form integrating leader-and-group call-and-response across rice-paddy-planting, fishing, boat-rowing, and other labor-contexts. Regional variants include the Northern Hò Sông Mã (Ma River boat-song), the Central Hò Đối-Đáp (call-and-response question-and-answer hò of central Vietnam), the Southern Hò Cấy (rice-planting hò of the Mekong Delta). Defined by unaccompanied call-and-response leader-and-group vocal arrangement, Vietnamese-language tonal-language-constrained vocal-melody, characteristic Vietnamese-folk pentatonic vocabulary, task-coordination labor-context.',
    exemplars: ['Hò Sông Mã (Ma River boat-song) canonical Northern-Vietnamese hò', 'Hò Đối-Đáp (call-and-response hò) canonical Central-Vietnamese', 'Hò Cấy (rice-planting hò) canonical Southern-Vietnamese Mekong-Delta', 'Hò Mái Nhì canonical Hue-region rowing-hò', 'Vietnamese rural-village hò continuous-living tradition'],
    crossRefs: ['fieldWork.southAsian', 'seaShanty.atlantic', 'protestSong.eastAsian'],
    status: 'documented',
