    description: 'The Romanian spinning-song (cântece de tors) tradition continuous from premodern Romanian-rural domestic-textile-labor practice (the wool-and-flax-spinning context where Romanian women performed evening spinning-bee gatherings called șezătoare in the documented social-context of multi-generational-household evening gatherings) through 19th-century Romanian-folklorist documentation through 20th-century Béla Bartók Romanian-folk-collection canonical into modern Romanian-folk-revival continuous practice. The Romanian șezătoare context integrated spinning-labor with extended narrative-song-and-doina performance. Defined by unaccompanied women\'s-solo-or-small-group vocal arrangement, Romanian-language text register, characteristic Romanian-folk modal vocabulary, characteristic narrow-range narrative-style.',
