  "bluegrass_fiddle": {"parent":"improvOnFrame.bluegrass","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":0,"ornament":1,"meter":1,"density":-1,"transmission":-1,"improv":1,"soundTech":-1,"intensity":0,"voice":-2,"timbre":0,"percussion":-1,"cyclicity":0},"description":"This instrument-focused branch brings the fiddle tune, melodic variation and sustained bowed phrasing to the front. Baker’s documented long-bow playing supplies the example; the authored acoustic backing uses mandolin, rhythm guitar and plucked bass. It can participate in vocal bluegrass too, but the default is an instrumental feature rather than a mandatory full-band solo rotation.","exemplars":["Kenny Baker","Kenny Baker plays Bill Monroe"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
