  "australian_country": {"parent":"functionalSong.country","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":0,"ornament":0,"meter":1,"density":0,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":0,"intensity":-1,"voice":2,"timbre":0,"percussion":0,"cyclicity":0},"description":"The authored default foregrounds a distinct lead voice over acoustic rhythm guitar, electric-guitar responses, bass and a restrained drum kit. This compact contemporary band is one national country branch; it does not pretend the older bush ballad, Aboriginal country, or every crossover production uses the same lineup.","exemplars":["Kasey Chambers — The Captain","Kasey Chambers — Bittersweet"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "australian_indie_folk": {"parent":"balladPoetry.angloSingerSong.indieFolk","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":0,"ornament":0,"meter":1,"density":0,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":0,"intensity":-1,"voice":2,"timbre":0,"percussion":-1,"cyclicity":0},"description":"Warm acoustic-guitar figures support layered voices, with banjo color and restrained bass-and-drums accompaniment. These roles come from The Paper Kites’ documented instrumental lineup, while the exact intimate balance is authored. The category allows studio textures and electric expansion rather than prescribing an entirely unplugged sound.","exemplars":["The Paper Kites — Woodland","The Paper Kites — Roses"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "australian_singer_songwriter": {"parent":"balladPoetry.angloSingerSong","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":0,"ornament":0,"meter":0,"density":-1,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":-1,"intensity":-1,"voice":2,"timbre":0,"percussion":-1,"cyclicity":0},"description":"The selected arrangement is voice with responsive piano and softly picked guitar, giving narrative phrasing and chord movement room to carry the song. Kelly’s collaborations include both guitar-led and piano-led settings; combining those resources here is an authored small arrangement, not an assertion about one session.","exemplars":["Paul Kelly","Paul Kelly and Paul Grabowsky — Please Leave Your Light On"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "belgian_singer_songwriter": {"parent":"balladPoetry.angloSingerSong","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":0,"ornament":0,"meter":0,"density":-1,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":-1,"intensity":-1,"voice":2,"timbre":0,"percussion":-1,"cyclicity":0},"description":"A lyric-and-melody-forward solo voice sits over acoustic guitar, with little masking texture. The arrangement follows Milow’s stated preference for sparseness while remaining one example within a multilingual Belgian category. Authorship rather than acoustic instrumentation alone distinguishes the label.","exemplars":["Milow — You Don’t Know"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
