  "canadian_indie_folk": {"parent":"balladPoetry.angloSingerSong.indieFolk","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":0,"ornament":0,"meter":0,"density":-1,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":0,"intensity":-1,"voice":2,"timbre":0,"percussion":-1,"cyclicity":0},"description":"A hushed lead voice and acoustic-guitar figure are colored by melodic fiddle and a restrained plucked bass. The default preserves the group’s documented folk-centered intimacy and spatial character while using a small selection of their broader acoustic/electric palette. These are production decisions, not claims that every Canadian indie-folk record uses historic rural rooms.","exemplars":["Great Lake Swimmers","Tony Dekker"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "canadian_americana": {"parent":"functionalSong.country.americana","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":0,"ornament":0,"meter":1,"density":0,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":0,"intensity":-1,"voice":2,"timbre":0,"percussion":-1,"cyclicity":0},"description":"Lead singing and ringing rhythm guitar are answered by pedal-steel swells and a simple plucked bass pulse. The authored setting draws on the band’s documented steel-and-guitar resources, selecting a country-rooted texture within a wider Canadian Americana field. It is not a claim that the entire category originated in one province.","exemplars":["Great Lake Swimmers — Caught Light"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "children_s_folk": {"parent":"nurseryRhyme","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":0,"ornament":0,"meter":1,"density":-1,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":-1,"intensity":-1,"voice":2,"timbre":0,"percussion":-1,"cyclicity":1},"description":"The default pairs an inviting lead-and-response voice arrangement with open-back banjo and strummed acoustic guitar. Clear recurring melodies and shared refrains make participation central. This is one recorded branch of children’s folk, not a universal claim about children’s repertoires across cultures or a label for all commercial children’s pop.","exemplars":["Pete Seeger — Folk Songs for Young People"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
