  "contemporary_folk": {"parent":"balladPoetry.angloSingerSong","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":0,"ornament":0,"meter":1,"density":0,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":0,"intensity":-1,"voice":2,"timbre":0,"percussion":-1,"cyclicity":0},"description":"The selected guitar-centered branch follows Cockburn’s documented acoustic and electric songwriting practice. Lead singing and fingerpicked guitar retain rhythmic detail, with restrained bass and drums providing an authored small-band setting. The category includes varied lyric subjects and production scales rather than one mandatory intimate solo sound.","exemplars":["Bruce Cockburn","John Gorka","Kate Wolf"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "canadian_country": {"parent":"functionalSong.country","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":0,"ornament":0,"meter":1,"density":1,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":1,"intensity":0,"voice":2,"timbre":0,"percussion":1,"cyclicity":0},"description":"Lead singing, acoustic and electric guitars, fiddle and pedal steel sit over a programmed rhythm foundation. This authored arrangement takes its instrumental resources from the documented country version of Up!, without claiming to recreate its exact session or to define all Canadian country by pop crossover.","exemplars":["Shania Twain — Up!"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "canadian_contemporary_country": {"parent":"functionalSong.country.contempMain","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":0,"ornament":0,"meter":1,"density":0,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":-1,"intensity":-1,"voice":2,"timbre":0,"percussion":0,"cyclicity":0},"description":"Voice, acoustic guitar, mandolin, plucked upright bass and restrained drums support a concise character-driven country song. This is an authored small-band realization of the acoustic resources documented for El Viejo; modern recording keeps rhythmic interaction clear. The wider roster contains contrasting contemporary approaches.","exemplars":["Corb Lund — El Viejo","Colter Wall","Terri Clark"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "deep_contemporary_country": {"parent":"functionalSong.country.contempMain","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":0,"ornament":0,"meter":1,"density":0,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":0,"intensity":-1,"voice":2,"timbre":0,"percussion":0,"cyclicity":0},"description":"The selected Kathy Mattea studio branch places lead and harmony voices above acoustic rhythm guitar, piano, pedal steel, bass and drums. Her official album credits document these roles; the authored model is a compact country band rather than a reproduction of any exact recording.","exemplars":["Kathy Mattea","Linda Davis","Rick Trevino"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "country_road": {"parent":"functionalSong.country.contempMain","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":0,"ornament":0,"meter":1,"density":1,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":0,"intensity":0,"voice":2,"timbre":0,"percussion":1,"cyclicity":0},"description":"Harmony-capable lead voices, piano and acoustic guitar sit above electric bass and a full drum groove. The authored default follows documented Lady A production centered on real ensemble playing and guitar/piano parts, keeping a direct song form and audible rhythmic support. The label does not require road-trip lyrics or designate a geographic birthplace.","exemplars":["Lady A","Luke Bryan","George Strait"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "baltic_folk": {"parent":"improvOnFrame","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":0,"ornament":1,"meter":0,"density":-1,"transmission":-1,"improv":1,"soundTech":-1,"intensity":-1,"voice":-2,"timbre":0,"percussion":-1,"cyclicity":1},"description":"Plucked kokle strings carry a decorated melody among ringing tones and selectively damped rhythmic figures. Repeated modal shapes provide a frame for changing accents, ornament and melodic variation in an intimate solo texture.","exemplars":["Laima Jansone"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "czech_country": {"parent":"functionalSong.country","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":0,"ornament":0,"meter":1,"density":0,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":-1,"intensity":-1,"voice":2,"timbre":0,"percussion":0,"cyclicity":0},"description":"Narrative singing is carried by acoustic rhythm guitar, five-string banjo and a resonator-guitar answering line over a plucked bass pulse. The chosen arrangement follows instruments documented among Greenhorns players; it keeps song accompaniment central rather than forcing every piece into a fast instrumental bluegrass break.","exemplars":["Greenhorns","Michal Tučný","Tomáš Linka"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
