  "finnish_dance_pop": {"parent":"functionalSong.europop","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":1,"ornament":0,"meter":2,"density":1,"transmission":2,"improv":-1,"soundTech":2,"intensity":1,"voice":2,"timbre":1,"percussion":2,"cyclicity":2},"description":"Finnish-language dance-pop represented by Antti Tuisku’s En kommentoi period and Peto on irti. The authored production combines a sung lead and overdubbed backing with a keyboard synthesizer and sampled programmed rhythm, following credited keyboard/programming/vocal roles. Exact synthesizer and sampler types are contemporary design choices. Separately credited human handclaps remain a distinct body-percussion instrument rather than being silently relabeled as drum samples.","exemplars":["Antti Tuisku — Peto on irti, En kommentoi (2015)"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "colombian_pop": {"parent":"functionalSong.popRock","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":1,"ornament":0,"meter":1,"density":1,"transmission":1,"improv":0,"soundTech":0,"intensity":1,"voice":2,"timbre":1,"percussion":2,"cyclicity":1},"description":"The three horn types remain distinct, including the credited tenor saxophone omitted from the earlier proposal. Congas provide an authored realization of the separate percussion role, while a grand-piano card realizes unspecified keyboards. Those subtype choices are not claimed as a verified inventory of every instrument physically present at Tiny Desk.","exemplars":["Juanes — Nada valgo sin tu amor (Tiny Desk, 2024)"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "classic_czech_pop": {"parent":"functionalSong.popRock","axes":{"harm":1,"pitch":1,"ornament":0,"meter":1,"density":-2,"transmission":0,"improv":0,"soundTech":-1,"intensity":-1,"voice":2,"timbre":0,"percussion":-2,"cyclicity":0},"description":"Historical Czech commercial popular song is represented here by Jiří Korn’s 1971 Yvetta, a Karel Svoboda composition with Zdeněk Rytíř text recorded with the Czechoslovak Radio Dance Orchestra. This deliberately reduced present-day vocal-and-violin arrangement extracts two explicitly credited melodic roles, using violin responses around the sung tune; it is not a reconstruction of the orchestra.","exemplars":["Jiří Korn — Yvetta (1971)"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
