  "afrikaans_hip_hop": {"parent":"mcRhythm.intlHipHop","axes":{"harm":-1,"pitch":0,"ornament":0,"meter":2,"density":-1,"transmission":1,"improv":1,"soundTech":1,"intensity":1,"voice":2,"timbre":0,"percussion":2,"cyclicity":2},"description":"The selected Cooler as Ekke verse uses conversational rhythmic rap against the sparse acoustic-guitar and drum-kit backing identified in the published musicological analysis. This is deliberately not a generic sampler-and-808 preset. The OM body, spruce/rosewood, fingerpicked articulation and maple kit are authored ways to realize the documented guitar/drum roles, not identified session specifications. The preset selects the rap verse; the additional sung female refrain is acknowledged but is not collapsed into the same spoken-flow voice setting.","exemplars":["Jack Parow — Cooler as Ekke (2009/2010), selected rap-verse texture"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "atl_hip_hop": {"parent":"mcRhythm.usHipHop.southern","axes":{"harm":1,"pitch":0,"ornament":0,"meter":2,"density":0,"transmission":1,"improv":1,"soundTech":2,"intensity":0,"voice":2,"timbre":1,"percussion":2,"cyclicity":2},"description":"The selected core of So Fresh, So Clean combines a rap verse, programmed drum beat, played electric bass and Rhodes chords. Sleepy Brown describes beginning on Rhodes and adding the beat and Preston’s bass line. This preset realizes that core groove, not a complete multitrack transcription: its sung hook, string/lead embellishments and different tracks across Stankonia are not claimed as fully represented. Exact bass construction, Rhodes model, drum-sample resolution and studio chain are authored recording defaults.","exemplars":["OutKast — So Fresh, So Clean (2000), core verse groove"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
