  "classic_nz_pop": {"parent":"functionalSong.popRock","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":1,"ornament":0,"meter":1,"density":0,"transmission":1,"improv":-1,"soundTech":0,"intensity":1,"voice":2,"timbre":0,"percussion":1,"cyclicity":1},"description":"New Zealand’s historical chart and television pop scene, with a selected early-1960s beat-group model. Te Ara documents independent labels, teen clubs, local television, R&B and Shadows-influenced guitars; the wider scene also contained country-pop, vocalists and psychedelic groups. This model is a contemporary realization of the documented practice, not a historical studio reconstruction.","exemplars":["Ray Columbus and the Invaders — She’s a Mod"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "classic_persian_pop": {"parent":"functionalSong.midEastNAfricanPop","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":1,"ornament":1,"meter":0,"density":-1,"transmission":1,"improv":-1,"soundTech":0,"intensity":-1,"voice":2,"timbre":1,"percussion":-2,"cyclicity":0},"description":"Historical Iranian popular-song repertoire associated with Googoosh and other pre-1979 stars. This selected new chamber rendition follows a documented Lalaee arrangement for countertenor, cello and piano, while retaining Googoosh as the repertoire exemplar. It does not assign that instrumentation or vocal range to her original recording. The primary concert programmes distinguish the later interpreters and name the arrangement explicitly. Bowed cello and piano support a developed high-register solo voice; exact materials and modern recording choices are authored.","exemplars":["Googoosh — Lalaee; contemporary arrangement performed by Cameron Shahbazi, Sophia Eva Muñoz and Eno Nushi"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "classic_peruvian_pop": {"parent":"functionalSong.popRock","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":1,"ornament":0,"meter":1,"density":1,"transmission":1,"improv":-1,"soundTech":1,"intensity":1,"voice":2,"timbre":1,"percussion":1,"cyclicity":1},"description":"Peruvian historical mainstream pop-rock represented by late-1980s Arena Hash: voice, guitar, keyboard, bass and drums within Lima radio and recording culture. This selected band strand does not equate Peruvian pop with Andean folk instrumentation. This model is a contemporary realization of the documented practice, not a historical studio reconstruction.","exemplars":["Arena Hash — Cuando la cama me da vueltas"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "classic_uk_pop": {"parent":"functionalSong.popRock","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":1,"ornament":0,"meter":1,"density":-1,"transmission":1,"improv":-1,"soundTech":0,"intensity":-1,"voice":2,"timbre":0,"percussion":0,"cyclicity":1},"description":"Historical UK mainstream chart, film and television pop, represented by the early Cliff Richard and Shadows singer-with-band practice. A relaxed guitar-led pop-song ensemble is selected; orchestral ballads and later decades remain within the wider category but are not reconstructed here. This model is a contemporary realization of the documented practice, not a historical studio reconstruction. This new arrangement gives lead guitar and strummed rhythm separate instrument colors: electric single-coil and acoustic steel-string. It does not claim that the Living Doll session used a Stratocaster; that specific historic lead instrument is deliberately left unasserted.","exemplars":["Cliff Richard and the Shadows — Travellin’ Light"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "classic_venezuelan_pop": {"parent":"functionalSong.popRock","axes":{"harm":1,"pitch":1,"ornament":0,"meter":0,"density":-2,"transmission":1,"improv":-1,"soundTech":0,"intensity":-1,"voice":2,"timbre":-1,"percussion":-2,"cyclicity":0},"description":"Venezuelan historical popular song represented by Franco De Vita’s 1980s Spanish-language piano ballad practice and television exposure. The authored reduction retains sung melody and piano accompaniment; it does not assert that the commercial recordings lacked other instruments. This model is a contemporary realization of the documented practice, not a historical studio reconstruction.","exemplars":["Franco De Vita — Sólo importas tú"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
