  "comic_metal": {"parent":"distortedRock.metal","axes":{"harm":1,"pitch":0,"ornament":1,"meter":0,"density":1,"transmission":0,"improv":0,"soundTech":1,"intensity":1,"voice":2,"timbre":1,"percussion":1,"cyclicity":1},"description":"Comic metal is retained as the source discovery label, whose roster spans parody, theatrical and humorous metal-adjacent acts. Nanowar of Steel supplies this explicit comedy-metal branch: a heavy-metal rhythm section supports theatrical sung exchanges and genre parody. The musicians describe humor as the project’s founding purpose, while the label documents polished metal parody. This authored guitar, bass, drums and two-voice model represents a band-centered branch; it does not declare every roster artist a parody act or invent a single comic-metal instrument formula.","exemplars":["Nanowar of Steel — band-centered comedy-metal branch"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "cosmic_death_metal": {"parent":"distortedRock.metal.death","axes":{"harm":1,"pitch":0,"ornament":1,"meter":2,"density":2,"transmission":0,"improv":0,"soundTech":2,"intensity":2,"voice":1,"timbre":1,"percussion":2,"cyclicity":1},"description":"Cosmic death metal is used here for the documented psychedelic/progressive death-metal field, with Blood Incantation’s Absolute Elsewhere as a selected branch. The record juxtaposes heavy guitar, fretless bass and drums with synthesizer textures. The band and producer describe extended ensemble preparation, drums tracked to tape then transferred to a DAW, and a Moog synthesizer beneath heavy sections. This authored five-role model emphasizes that metal/electronic contrast rather than treating the band’s wholly ambient Timewave Zero as death metal.","exemplars":["Blood Incantation — Absolute Elsewhere (2024), heavy-band/synth branch"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
