  "russian_folk_metal": {"parent":"distortedRock.metal.folkMetal","axes":{"harm":1,"pitch":1,"ornament":2,"meter":1,"density":2,"transmission":0,"improv":0,"soundTech":1,"intensity":2,"voice":2,"timbre":1,"percussion":2,"cyclicity":2},"description":"Russian folk metal is represented by a selected whistle-bearing Arkona arrangement. The label documents voice, electric and acoustic guitars, bass, drum kit, keyboards and a multi-instrumental wind role. This realization selects tin whistle from that wider wind palette, without claiming every listed wind instrument sounds at once or reproducing one album in full. Exact studio chain, tuning and part selections are contemporary authored production choices.","exemplars":["Arkona"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
